What is Bulk Material Transportation?
Bulk material transportation refers to the movement of large volumes of unpackaged, homogeneous commodities that are typically handled in a “unit‑load” or “bulk” fashion rather than as individual parcels. Unlike containerised freight, bulk shipments are loaded directly into specialised equipment such as hopper trucks, railcars, barges or pipelines, allowing for rapid loading and unloading cycles. The market serves critical downstream industries-including construction, mining, agriculture and heavy manufacturing-where timely delivery of raw inputs is a prerequisite for continuous production and project execution.
